# PROJECT: AgriShare
Farm equipment rental platform. Small farmers rent machines from owners.
Responsive website and installable PWA from one codebase. Six languages.
Every tool and service must be free.

Work in phases. Finish each phase completely before starting the next.
Do not write test files or run test suites. Do not stop to ask questions;
make reasonable decisions and record them in docs/DECISIONS.md.

## 0. RULES
- Every dependency free and open source. No paid APIs or SaaS.
- No placeholder code, no TODO stubs, no "implement later". Every listed feature works.
- No hardcoded secrets. Use .env with .env.example.
- All user-facing strings go through i18n. No hardcoded English in components.
- Money is integer paise everywhere. Never floats.
- Code is typed, consistently formatted, and commented where logic is non-obvious.

## 1. STACK (fixed)
Client (/client): React 18, Vite, TypeScript, Tailwind CSS, React Router v6,
TanStack Query, Zustand, react-i18next + i18next, Leaflet + OpenStreetMap,
vite-plugin-pwa, Framer Motion, Lucide React.

Server (/server): Node 20, Express, TypeScript, Prisma, PostgreSQL 16,
jsonwebtoken, bcryptjs, Zod, Multer, Sharp, node-cron, Helmet, cors,
express-rate-limit, Pino.

Shared (/shared): constants.ts and types.ts used by both sides.

Distance: Haversine in dsa/geo.ts. Road distance via Dijkstra over the
location graph. Optional OSRM demo server with Haversine fallback.

Payments: internal double-entry wallet. PaymentProvider interface with a
MockProvider that marks top-ups successful immediately.

