### PHASE 1: Database (Prisma)
Models:
- User: id, name, phone (unique), email?, passwordHash, role, language
  (default "en"), village, district, state, latitude, longitude, isSuspended,
  suspendedUntil, trustScore (float, default 5.0), createdAt
- Machine: id, ownerId, name, category, description, capabilities (string[]),
  brand, modelYear, horsepower, pricePerHour (paise int), minHours, deposit
  (paise int), locationId, isActive, createdAt
- MachineImage: id, machineId, url, sortOrder
- Location: id, name, latitude, longitude, district, state
- LocationEdge: id, fromLocationId, toLocationId, distanceKm (undirected)
- Availability: id, machineId, startTime, endTime, isBlocked
- Booking: id, machineId, farmerId, startTime, endTime, status (PENDING,
  CONFIRMED, ACTIVE, RETURNED, LATE, CANCELLED, COMPLETED), totalAmount,
  depositAmount, lateFeeAmount (default 0), returnedAt, createdAt
- Wallet: id, userId (unique), balance (paise, never negative)
- LedgerEntry: id, walletId, amount (signed paise), type (TOPUP,
  BOOKING_HOLD, BOOKING_RELEASE, EARNING, LATE_FEE, DEPOSIT_REFUND,
  DEPOSIT_FORFEIT), referenceId, createdAt
- Rating: id, bookingId (unique), raterId, rateeId, score (1-5), comment, createdAt
- Penalty: id, userId, bookingId?, type (LATE_RETURN, DAMAGE, NO_SHOW),
  severity, note, createdAt
- Warning: id, userId, reason, createdAt
- Notification: id, userId, messageKey, params (json), isRead, createdAt

Indexes: Booking(machineId, startTime, endTime), Machine(category, isActive),
Location(latitude, longitude), Penalty(userId).

seed.ts: 4 owners, 8 farmers, 3 admins, 30 machines (images from local
placeholder files in uploads/seed/), 40 locations in a grid, edges between
neighbors, wallets for all users.
Done when: migration runs and seed completes.

### PHASE 2: DSA engine (pure TypeScript, server/src/dsa/)
No framework imports. Each file has a header comment with algorithm name,
time complexity, and space complexity. Each export is typed and documented.

1. trie.ts: insert, prefix search up to N results. Case-insensitive.
   Handles Devanagari and Kannada by iterating code points.
2. maxHeap.ts: generic binary heap with comparator. push, pop, peek, size.
3. graph.ts: adjacency-list undirected weighted graph. addNode, addEdge, neighbors.
4. dijkstra.ts: single-source shortest distances using maxHeap as min-heap
   (inverted comparator). Returns distance and predecessor maps. Path
   reconstruction function.
5. intervalIndex.ts: sorted-by-start interval list per machine. add, remove,
   hasOverlap(start, end) via binary search, findFreeSlots(start, end, minMinutes).
   Half-open intervals [start, end).
6. bookingQueue.ts: FIFO queue per machine. enqueue, dequeue, peek, size.
7. rankingEngine.ts: min-max normalization with divide-by-zero guard. Three views:
   CHEAPEST (by price), NEAREST (by distance), BALANCED (weighted score).
   Top-K via maxHeap in O(n log K). Weights from request, normalized to sum 1.
   Score: wPrice*(1-normPrice) + wDistance*(1-normDistance) + wRating*normRating.
   Each result includes a plain-language reason string.
8. geo.ts: haversine in km, guard for identical points.

Also write DSA_NOTES.md with complexity for every function.
Done when: everything compiles and every export has its header.

### PHASE 3: Backend API
Global: Express with Helmet, CORS (CLIENT_URL), JSON limit 1mb,
express-rate-limit on /auth, global error handler returning
{ error: { code, message } } via ApiError, Zod validation on every route,
Pino request logging, static /uploads.

Auth:
- POST /auth/register (name, phone, password, role, village, district, state, language)
- POST /auth/login (phone, password) returns JWT
- GET /auth/me
- Password min 8 chars, bcrypt cost 12.

Users: GET and PATCH /users/me (profile, language, location, password).

Machines (owner):
- POST /machines (multipart, up to 6 images, Sharp to 1280px WebP)
- GET /machines/mine, PATCH /machines/:id
- DELETE /machines/:id (soft delete, blocked if future bookings exist)
- POST /machines/:id/availability (block windows)

Search (farmer):
- GET /search/suggest?q= (trie, up to 8 names)
- GET /search?category&query&lat&lng&radiusKm&startTime&endTime&sort
  Filter active machines, drop conflicts via intervalIndex, compute distance
  (haversine, or Dijkstra when both endpoints are graph nodes), return three
  views from rankingEngine. Accept priceWeight, distanceWeight, ratingWeight.
  Each result: machine, price, distance, rating, score, reason string.

Bookings:
- POST /bookings: through bookingQueue per machine. Check intervalIndex,
  check wallet covers amount + deposit, BOOKING_HOLD ledger entry, status
  CONFIRMED. Respect minHours.
- GET /bookings/mine (farmer), GET /bookings/requests (owner)
- PATCH /bookings/:id/start (owner marks handover, ACTIVE)
- PATCH /bookings/:id/return (owner marks return; compute lateness, LATE_FEE,
  release or forfeit deposit)
- PATCH /bookings/:id/cancel (full refund if more than 24h before start, 50% otherwise)
- On COMPLETED: EARNING credit to owner.

Wallet:
- GET /wallet, POST /wallet/topup (via PaymentProvider)
- Every money move: two ledger entries in one Prisma transaction. Balance
  checked inside the transaction.

Penalties:
- Late fee per started hour, from constants.ts.
- First late return: warning. Three within 30 days: 7-day suspension.
- Owner damage report with note.
- Suspended users cannot book or list machines.

Ratings: POST /ratings after COMPLETED, once per booking, moving average on trustScore.

Admin: GET /admin/overview, GET /admin/users, POST /admin/users/:id/suspend,
POST /admin/users/:id/unsuspend, GET /admin/penalties.

Scheduler (node-cron): every 15 min, ACTIVE past endTime become LATE with
LATE_RETURN penalty and warning. Daily, expire stale PENDING bookings.

Done when: server starts, all routes mounted, TypeScript compiles.

### PHASE 4: Design system
Earthy, trustworthy, modern. Not a generic template.
- Light palette: primary #1F4D2B, accent #E0A526, secondary text #6B4A2F,
  background #FBF8EF, surface #FFFFFF, danger #B3261E, success #2E7D32.
- Dark palette: background #0F1A12, surface #17251B, text #EDE8D8.
  Defined as CSS variables in theme.css. Toggle stored in localStorage.
- Fonts (Google Fonts): Noto Sans, Noto Sans Devanagari (hi, mr), Noto Sans
  Kannada, Noto Sans Tamil, Noto Sans Telugu. Base 17px.
- Tap targets minimum 44px. High contrast for outdoor use.
- Components: 14px radius, soft shadows, Framer Motion fade and slide,
  respecting prefers-reduced-motion.
- Lucide icons only. Skeleton loaders, empty states, and toasts on every async action.

### PHASE 5: Frontend pages and flows
Routes:
- Public: /, /login, /register
- Farmer: /search, /search/:machineId, /bookings, /wallet
- Owner: /owner, /owner/machines, /owner/machines/new, /owner/requests, /owner/earnings
- Admin: /admin, /admin/users, /admin/penalties
- Shared: /profile
Role guards via RequireRole. Unauthorized redirects to /login.

Landing: hero "Rent the machine. Skip the purchase.", three steps with icons,
live count of available machines, language switcher visible, one CTA per role.

Register: language first, then role as two large cards ("I farm" / "I own
machines"), one field per step on mobile.

Farmer search: debounced autocomplete. Filter panel (category chips, radius
slider, date and time). Geolocation if allowed, else typed village. Three tabs:
Cheapest, Nearest, Best Balance, each showing the reason line. Weight slider
with live re-ranking. Map toggle with Leaflet.

Machine detail: swipeable gallery, capability tags, owner rating, price per
hour and deposit shown clearly, slot picker, confirmation showing total,
deposit, and late-return rule in plain words.

Owner: Dashboard (active bookings, monthly earnings, utilization). Add machine
(multi-step: basics, capabilities, pricing, photos with reorder, map pin).
Requests (Accept, Handover, Returned, damage report). Earnings ledger.

Farmer bookings: timeline with status badges, cancel with refund preview.
Wallet: balance card, top-up, history.
Admin: stat cards, user table with search and suspend, penalty log.
Profile: language, location, password.

UX rules: inline validation in active language. Loading, success, and error
states on every async action. Money as ₹ with Indian digit grouping.
Distances in km, one decimal. Dates in user's locale.

